  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342225",
      "title": "The Deno Runtime (Namespace) API",
      "lectureOrder": 520,
      "videoOrder": 461,
      "sourceHash": "72d5ae94c76a0af18cfcb3f0cf590b0e86fda145f4b2f0318d47dcb91340141b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.14,
          "en": "As mentioned, when you're working with Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.14,
          "end": 8.21,
          "en": "you have these core Node modules here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.21,
          "end": 12.02,
          "en": "for example, a module for working with the file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.02,
          "end": 15.34,
          "en": "and with Node, you simply import such a module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.34,
          "end": 20.2,
          "en": "and then you can start reading or writing files for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.2,
          "end": 24.1,
          "en": "As you learned in the modern Java script with Node module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.1,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "you also have a promise based API version available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 30.56,
          "en": "for some of these core modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.56,
          "end": 33.88,
          "en": "Now for Deno, we have a similar concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.88,
          "end": 37.963,
          "en": "There we have this so-called runtime API here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.83,
          "end": 42.59,
          "en": "also sometimes called the namespace APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.59,
          "end": 46.57,
          "en": "These are core APIs, core features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.57,
          "end": 48.8,
          "en": "which are built into Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.8,
          "end": 52.76,
          "en": "and which are available on a Deno object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.76,
          "end": 55.75,
          "en": "which in turn is globally available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.75,
          "end": 58.97,
          "en": "in any Deno code you're executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.97,
          "end": 62.81,
          "en": "And here you got core modules for working with files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.81,
          "end": 65.17,
          "en": "for working with requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.17,
          "end": 69.27,
          "en": "You also got core features like set timeouts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 71.92,
          "en": "set interval, clear timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.92,
          "end": 74.06,
          "en": "You have to fetch API available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.06,
          "end": 75.97,
          "en": "for sending network requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.97,
          "end": 77.65,
          "en": "And that actually by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.65,
          "end": 80.83,
          "en": "is a difference compared to Node already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.83,
          "end": 81.69,
          "en": "In Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.69,
          "end": 85.61,
          "en": "You also have some core APIs available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.61,
          "end": 87.76,
          "en": "some core features available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.76,
          "end": 92.50999999999999,
          "en": "either after importing them from the respective core module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.50999999999999,
          "end": 94.75,
          "en": "or things like set timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.75,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "also are globally available in Node scripts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 102.7,
          "en": "but things like the fetch API are not available in Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.7,
          "end": 105.4,
          "en": "because Deno has the core philosophy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.4,
          "end": 109.12,
          "en": "of being as browser compatible as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.12,
          "end": 113.15,
          "en": "That means that any code that could run outside of a browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.15,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "is also supported in Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 119.57,
          "en": "Something like the fetch API for sending HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.57,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "This is a available in Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.78,
          "en": "because this is not strictly tied to a browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.78,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "Of course we can send a fetch request at HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "from any Java script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 132.89,
          "en": "Now, of course, there also are other features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.89,
          "end": 135.5,
          "en": "for example, related to writing files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.5,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "which exist in Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "because Deno runs out sort of a browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 142.86,
          "en": "but which wouldn't exist inside of a browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.86,
          "end": 145.87,
          "en": "And there are features which we can use in a browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.87,
          "end": 149.8,
          "en": "for example, features to interact with the browser Dom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.8,
          "end": 152.48,
          "en": "which are not supported in Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.48,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "Also not supported in Node of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 157.18,
          "en": "because there we have no Dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.18,
          "end": 159.88,
          "en": "there we are not running inside of a browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.88,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "So that's how you can think about these core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 166.52,
          "en": "It's basically what you can do in the browser minus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.52,
          "end": 169.32999999999998,
          "en": "features that only makes sense in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.32999999999998,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "plus features that can't be used inside of the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 175.34,
          "en": "that can be used outside of it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.34,
          "end": 177.89,
          "en": "Something like writing files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.89,
          "end": 181.31,
          "en": "And with that, I say, we talked about this enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.31,
          "end": 183.6,
          "en": "let's now write some Deno code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 185.5,
          "en": "and let's see how we can utilize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.5,
          "end": 188.04,
          "en": "these built-in core features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.04,
          "end": 190.983,
          "en": "These namespace API features.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
